--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Map tiles  —  gcs/tiles/  (1996 files, z9-z19, ~41 MB)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Esri ArcGIS World Imagery, fetched from
https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}
by gcs/scripts/prefetch_tiles.py.

  Imagery (c) Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics, and the GIS User Community.

The console displays that attribution at runtime. The tiles are committed
because the console has to draw its map with NO INTERNET: the competition site
has no usable connectivity and the aircraft's own WiFi AP has no uplink, so a
tile that is not in the repository is a blank square on the day. They cover only
the three fields this project flew.

Esri's terms of use permit caching for offline use in limited circumstances and
do not clearly extend to redistributing a cached tile set. If you reuse this
repository, the clean path is to delete gcs/tiles/ and fetch your own:

    python3 gcs/scripts/prefetch_tiles.py --field <your field.yaml>

The console runs fine with no tiles at all — every overlay (pads, zones,
aircraft, planned route) renders over blank squares.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SITL ground texture  —  mission/sitl/models/ground_sat/materials/textures/sat_real.png
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A satellite image of the KMUTNB rooftop pitch used as the Gazebo ground plane,
produced by mission/tools/fetch_sat.py. That tool's default provider chain starts
at Google satellite imagery (mt1.google.com, z20) and falls back to Esri;
mission/README.md records this file as the Google z20 branch.

Google's Maps/Earth Additional Terms of Service prohibit mass download and
redistribution of their content. This file is COSMETIC — the simulation flies
identically without it. Regenerate it for your own site rather than reusing this
one:

    cd mission && python3 tools/fetch_sat.py --provider esri --zoom 19

